    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Same-restaurant sales are under visible strain, with traffic and mix headwinds eroding performance in existing locations, while commodity and labor cost inflation continue to pressure profitability. Offset this, the company is pushing into new geographies—Texas, Colorado, Nevada, and Georgia—and reinforcing its Chicago core. Analyst commentary reflects caution around execution and comp trends, yet acknowledges the brand’s appeal and multichannel potential, leaving a mixed but restless narrative.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** A new CEO has taken the helm amid a deliberate national expansion using a smaller “restaurant of the future” prototype. Pricing actions are being diluted by an unfavorable product mix, and margin erosion persists. Development milestones have at times lifted market mood, but downward analyst fair-value rework and missed EPS expectations point to growing skepticism about near‑term delivery. The evolving story centers on whether growth ambitions can coexist with stabilizing legacy operations and restoring execution credibility.",
